WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.080 --> 00:00:08.020
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and Oscar Isaac
has just been cast as Apocalypse in the next

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.050
X-Men Movie.

00:00:09.050 --> 00:00:19.320
Originally it was called Age of Apocalypse,
now the movie is just called Apocalypse.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:26.020
Oscar Isaac in case you forgot is one of the
main cast members of Star Wars Episode 7.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:30.039
It’s a little too soon to be calling him
the next Chris Pratt but maybe we can think

00:00:30.039 --> 00:00:31.750
of him as an evil Chris Pratt.

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:37.909
A small indie actor that suddenly blows up
playing villains in some of the biggest franchises

00:00:37.909 --> 00:00:38.909
in history.

00:00:38.909 --> 00:00:41.850
To be clear, we don’t know officially what
his Star Wars character is going to be.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:49.540
The rumors say scoundrel but I’ll talk more
about that during my Star Wars Trailer breakdown

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:50.760
on friday.

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:52.699
Today is all about Mutants.

00:00:52.699 --> 00:00:54.790
And we can actually use that word because
this is FOX.

00:00:54.790 --> 00:00:59.570
I get so tired of all the legal bullshit with
Fox using the word mutant and Marvel using

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:06.640
the word Inhuman to describe people humans
with special powers.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:15.340
Whatever, here’s what we know about the
movie so far.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:20.310
In order of importance to the narrative there’s
Apocalypse, it’s named after him, of course

00:01:20.310 --> 00:01:25.220
it’s going to be about his life, then Jennifer
Lawrence’s Mystique and Michael Fassbender’s

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:26.220
Magneto.

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:27.690
All the other young cast members will be back
from Days of Future Past.

00:01:27.690 --> 00:01:28.790
The ones that did not die that is.

00:01:28.790 --> 00:01:33.410
And the movie will take place in the near
future after the events of Days of Future

00:01:33.410 --> 00:01:34.410
Past.

00:01:34.410 --> 00:01:37.010
If that was in the 70s, just consider Age
of Apocalypse to be early mid 80s.

00:01:37.010 --> 00:01:40.530
The end credits teaser featured Apocalypse
in Ancient Egypt so there will be flashbacks

00:01:40.530 --> 00:01:41.790
explaining where he came from.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:44.580
But the majority of the movie will be in present
day.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:45.580
When the characters are all adults.

00:01:45.580 --> 00:01:48.280
The story was planned to be the next logical
step given the events of Days of Future Past.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:51.430
So magneto assaults the president on live
television with all the world watching.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:53.840
He’s taken down, but where do we go from
here.

00:01:53.840 --> 00:01:57.340
And what about the other end credits scene
where Wolverine wakes up in the alternate

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.120
timeline version of Professor X’s academy.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:00.430
The future where everyone is still alive?

00:02:00.430 --> 00:02:03.850
The timeline is going to get fuzzier, but
it just implies that of course the X-Men will

00:02:03.850 --> 00:02:04.850
defeat apocalypse.

00:02:04.850 --> 00:02:07.610
The X-Men franchise is such a critical part
of Fox’s earnings as a company, that I don’t

00:02:07.610 --> 00:02:08.720
think they’d risk money by leaving things
on a super downer ending.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:09.720
The safe bet is always to give the protagonists
a big win.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:11.090
Unless it’s Empire Strikes Back and your
movie is part of a Trilogy.

00:02:11.090 --> 00:02:14.000
Which it kind of isn’t, the X-Men Franchise
isn’t really a trilogy right now.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:16.720
It’s just a new movie every couple of years
that are all loosely connected.

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:20.070
It’s not like Christopher Nolan’s Dark
Knight Trilogy where the beginning, middle

00:02:20.070 --> 00:02:22.240
and end are all meticulously planned in advance.

00:02:22.240 --> 00:02:33.170
If you haven’t read the Age of Apocalypse
Comic Book Story or seen the animated tv series

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:34.170
adaptation.

00:02:34.170 --> 00:02:42.000
As the name implies, it’s kind of like a
Days of Future Past situation where the world

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:46.210
is taken over by Apocalypse with the aid of
his four horsemen and Mr Sinister.

00:02:46.210 --> 00:02:50.180
Days of Future Past is all about what the
world would look like if Humanity tried to

00:02:50.180 --> 00:02:53.130
eradicate the Mutants, Age of Apocalypse is
the other side of that.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:57.760
Apocalypse as a character isn’t so much
a believer in Mutant Rights like Magneto,

00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.989
he preaches Survival of the Fittest.

00:03:01.989 --> 00:03:07.209
So if you can vaporize matter with eye beams,
in his eyes, you are deemed more worthy of

00:03:07.209 --> 00:03:09.260
the right to live in his new world order.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:14.510
Because they just did Time Travel in the last
movie, I don’t think they’ll do the exact

00:03:14.510 --> 00:03:15.510
same thing again.

00:03:15.510 --> 00:03:18.420
So I think they’ll change the comic book
story to eliminate the post-apocalyptic parts

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.950
and just keep it mostly in present day.

00:03:20.950 --> 00:03:24.900
Like the creation of the Four Horseman and
the X-Men fighting Apocalypse and Mr Sinister

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:25.900
to a standstill.

00:03:25.900 --> 00:03:28.200
The movie will probably be just as long as
Days of Future Past in terms of duration,

00:03:28.200 --> 00:03:31.900
which is well over two hours, so they’ll
have plenty of time to do a whole side story

00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:33.470
for Apocalypse and his four horsemen.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:36.349
Mr Sinister isn’t confirmed but I really
hope we see him.

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:39.651
And speaking of new X-Men characters, they’re
re-casting Cyclops, Jean Grey and the other

00:03:39.651 --> 00:03:41.110
X-Men that did not appear in First Class.

00:03:41.110 --> 00:03:44.440
I know they had young Cyclops in Wolverine
Origins, but they’re recasting all those

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:45.440
X-Men.

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:46.630
The First Class actors will still play their
characters.

00:03:46.630 --> 00:03:48.530
And then there’s the issue of Channing Tatum’s
Gambit.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:51.930
He’s getting his own Solo Film after Apocalypse
but he’s supposedly not going to be feature

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.200
in the big team up movie.

00:03:53.200 --> 00:04:00.080
It’s possible they could tease him, it would
make sense from a marketing standpoint.

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.310
But his character isn’t going to be a big
part of the film.

00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:04.430
Even though in the comics he did become one
of Apocalypse’s Horsemen.

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:07.270
He was Death, in the original comic that was
Warren Worthington.

00:04:07.270 --> 00:04:10.580
Everyone asking about Taylor Kitsch being
bumped from the role.

00:04:10.580 --> 00:04:15.890
Yes, I think if John Carter had not of been
such an epic flop he would still be Gambit.

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:18.129
Channing Tatum is guaranteed box office for
Fox though.

00:04:18.129 --> 00:04:21.129
I’m going to wait till I see footage to
pass judgement on that.

00:04:21.129 --> 00:04:28.949
There are tons of things you can do to get
ready for the 

00:04:28.949 --> 00:04:56.110
Apocalypse Movie though, first being read
the Original Age of Apocalypse 

00:04:56.110 --> 00:04:59.729
comic book.

00:04:59.729 --> 00:05:15.659
A 

00:05:15.659 --> 00:05:26.249
lot of aspects of that will be in the movie.

00:05:26.249 --> 00:05:29.949
It won’t be a straight up adaptation though.

00:05:29.949 --> 00:05:33.009
They changed a bunch of stuff about Days of
Future Past from the comics, so just expect

00:05:33.009 --> 00:05:37.139
the same thing to happen with the new movie.

00:05:37.139 --> 00:05:59.759
Right now Apocalypse is a big part of the
X-Men Avengers AXIS comic book story, so you

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:09.999
should check that out too.

00:06:09.999 --> 00:06:24.639
They did Hellfire Club in First Class and
in the comics Apocalypse meets Mister Sinister

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:38.052
through them, so they could bring the Club
back in the new movie.

00:06:38.052 --> 00:06:45.900
Age of Stryfe is a fun storyline.

00:06:45.900 --> 00:06:52.300
Right now in the comics the Apocalypse in
AXIS is the clone version.

00:06:52.300 --> 00:06:57.689
If you have any other big Apocalypse or Mister
Sinsiter comics you guys want to recommend

00:06:57.689 --> 00:07:00.839
just write them below in the comics.

00:07:00.839 --> 00:07:02.999
Here’s my big question for you.

00:07:02.999 --> 00:07:08.999
Do you think that Fox should join their Fantastic
Four movies with the X-Men Franchise.

00:07:08.999 --> 00:07:13.330
Do you think they can pull off the same shared
universe Marvel has?

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:23.770
The odds are against them and there are a
lot of bigger hollywood people that are firmly

00:07:23.770 --> 00:07:31.159
against this type of shared universe stuff
just because it places a lot of restrictions

00:07:31.159 --> 00:07:33.580
on what stories they can tell.

00:07:33.580 --> 00:07:55.110
It’s the difference between doing whatever
you want with a group of characters, versus

00:07:55.110 --> 00:08:13.949
being forced to write within the canon created
by other directors and writers.

00:08:13.949 --> 00:08:21.629
Regardless of whether you like what they did.

00:08:21.629 --> 00:08:25.369
Right now I kind of like that only Marvel
is doing it, I don’t think I’d want to

00:08:25.369 --> 00:08:30.169
see everyone else do it too.

